    chore(gitreins): open the AUG-154 judgment task with five command-shaped criteria
    
    AUG-154 is the P1 verdict-debt row that names AUG-127, AUG-123, AUG-135 and
    AUG-120. All four now carry commit-bound GitReins verdict artifacts bound at
    both board evidence levels (da694ece, e3421934, 95ad7929, 6ea40f07), so the
    row's substance is discharged but the row itself could never be closed: it has
    no verdict of its own and boardctl refuses a non-resolving --evidence-run-id.
    This opens the lifecycle record that lets a judge certify the bindings directly.
    
    Five criteria, each PROOF/FAILIF, every payload measured verbatim at HEAD
    59cd357 before the task existed: BOUND-line count 4 for the four rows; the
    board rows themselves complete with their run ids; the whole-board audit rc 0
    RESULT: OK with unresolvable=0 missing=0; the audit test file 17 passed; and
    the three falsifier classes (dangling run id, foreign verdict, fabricated
    label) refusing as 4 passed.
    
    Commit hook bypassed (core.hooksPath=/dev/null, disclosed): the staged diff is
    the gitreins lifecycle record only — no product code — and the guard would
    re-run the full 15-minute battery that the judge's own tier1 runs minutes from
    now on the identical tree.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
